}$, where $c_{1} = 5b_{2}$ and $c_{2} = 4b_{1}$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120532 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119825 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e568b6fc-88f0-592b-a24d-e3286cfa5043" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Vector in a Different Basis Given a Linear Relationship Between Two Bases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49f70848-64e2-5a94-90fd-e1f2b7e3d679" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345983} {:answer/id #uuid "6537a611-fcd7-568a-9601-b81937251d50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346233} {:answer/id #uuid "795d20fc-2f91-5397-8210-b27b01a471fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346414} {:answer/id #uuid "c3c43852-87af-51a6-be1f-90b3e59f2e27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347041} {:answer/id #uuid "dd2bb630-c228-5f6a-909a-e8010089efeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347289}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6537a611-fcd7-568a-9601-b81937251d50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346233} :answer-field/id #uuid "68e7d678-d060-59d1-9497-9ed2b25f012c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347787}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a2b67a92-2b23-5739-813e-476de8609802" :question/math-academy-id "q-80635" :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}},$ where ${c}_{1}={b}_{1}-2{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}={b}_{1}+{b}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We are given that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}={b}_{1}-2{b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2}={b}_{1}+{b}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the $b$'s in terms of $c$'s. Multiplying the second equation by $2$ and adding the equations, we get \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}=3{b}_{1}\\,⟹\\,{b}_{1}=\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{1}+\\frac{2}{3}{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=(\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{1}+\\frac{2}{3}{c}_{2})-2{b}_{2}\\,⟹\\,{b}_{2}=-\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSince $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$, we can write the vector $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2{b}_{1}-3{b}_{2} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{1}+\\frac{2}{3}{c}_{2})-3(-\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{c}_{1}+\\frac{4}{3}{c}_{2}+{c}_{1}-{c}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382414 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119825 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e568b6fc-88f0-592b-a24d-e3286cfa5043" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Vector in a Different Basis Given a Linear Relationship Between Two Bases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2801f550-4675-529c-9816-dd8a23db76c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident 